\title{Restricted sum}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2023-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{Returning to the topic of sumsets, this time we shall investigate \em{restricted sums} of sets. Given sets #{A, B \subset \mathbb{Z}_p}, at least how large is their sum if we demand that the summands are different. Thus, at least how large is}

##{A \oplus B = \lbrace a + b : a \in A, b \in B, a \neq b\rbrace ?}
